%description:

Tcp.rackReoTimerGranularity:exact -- RACK retransmits when the reordering window ends.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "model the kernel's jiffy-quantized REO timeout arming (Linux
usecs_to_jiffies(timeout)+1: delay rounded UP to this granularity plus one extra tick, e.g.
4ms for an HZ=250 kernel) ... 0 = exact".

The classes: exact (0 s, the default) and ticks (4 ms, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::rescheduleRackReoTimer() rounds a positive delay of the timer of the
reordering window up to the granularity and adds one tick, (ceil(delay / g) + 1) * g, when
the granularity is above 0. A value below 0 acts as 0; the NED names no such value. This test separates "exact" from "ticks".

Host under test: host1, with RACK and without the tail loss probe (precondition), which sends
three segments; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the first segment once. At the first duplicate ACK, the
reordering window is a quarter of the round trip, about 10 ms, and the timer of the
reordering window waits for it. Observation: level 1, the retransmission of the first segment comes 9 to 11 ms after the
first duplicate ACK.

%# parameter: Tcp.rackReoTimerGranularity
%# class: exact
%# value: 0s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.rackReoTimerGranularity
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpRackReoTimerGranularityExact")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the first data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1")
             .describe("the first duplicate ACK, which SACKs the second segment")
             .within(0.5))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early retransmission of the first segment, by the timer of RACK")
              .within(0.009))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("retransmission of the first segment, by the timer of RACK")
             .within(0.002));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpRackReoTimerGranularityExact compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.rackReoTimerGranularity = 0s    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 4344B
*.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpRackReoTimerGranularityExact: PASS
